        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-12T15:43:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I thought that was one of my better hacks :-)\n\nThe reason for putting it there is we go to some trouble to make sure that text is fully written before exiting the VM.\n\nWhen the failures occurred, none of the guest-side logging appeared. So I don\u0027t think that\u0027s a solution.\n\n(It occurs to me that we will get this fairly content-free error even if the app developer makes a trivial mistake like misspelling the binary name, so I think we need to do something.)",
      "parentUuid": "3640da1a_732eb158",
      "revId": "edd56fe63fe36a2224df47767ffca7ce1422e8f5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8ccf8173_4033569c",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-13T00:27:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually I think I wholly garbled that.\n\nI was surprised none of the VM logs appeared, but I suspected that may be due to debug not being enabled. I did try running with full debug, but then the bug failed to reproduce.\n\nSo I think actually, yes, I do want this even for non-debuggable. An alternative would be to add a bunch more error codes (or perhaps sub-codes), but that isn\u0027t really as good - I want to know what OS error happened and on what file and in what context.\n\nAs long as we think there\u0027s no significant risk of leaking secrets - and this is before the payload starts - I think something similar to this patch is the way forward. The details of the encoding are negotiable of course.\n\nAnd the extra context() calls would be useful regardless.",
      "parentUuid": "2838852d_4ec3cfa2",
      "revId": "edd56fe63fe36a2224df47767ffca7ce1422e8f5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
